{
  "_comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later. FORK: CADApp joint presets (design doc §5.1.1, Phase 5.1). A preset is a joinery rule without part names (see Joinery.py): kind, sizes in mm, fastener (hardware id), spacing / edge / per_joint for the count, operation ({n} = count; {s} / {es} = plural ending) and on (receiver, inserted, both). allows_movement: the joint lets solid wood move across its grain (checked for wide solid parts). fixes: false for joints that hold without fixing (shelf pins). meets lists how the two parts touch for the preset to be offered: end_to_face, face_to_face, edge_to_face, crossing. Copy an item to your user library under a new id to change sizes.",
  "source": "Common woodworking practice; original compilation, no maker's or book's table copied.",
